  "createdAt" : 1773781875,
  "description" : "This dataset contains the number and percent of students participating in the MCAS by each grade, subject and student group from 2017 onward.\n\nThe Massachusetts Comprehensive Assessment System (MCAS) is a statewide assessment administered to help parents, students, educators, and policymakers determine where districts, schools, and students are meeting expectations and where they need additional support. For more information about MCAS data, please visit the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education’s <a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/help/data.aspx?section=assess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Profiles Help - About the Data</a> page.\n\nThis dataset counts participation in both the current (“Next Gen”) MCAS assessment as well as the prior Legacy MCAS assessment. Results from different assessment systems measure different standards and cannot be directly compared. Please see the DESE Researcher’s Guide linked as featured content below for more information.\n\nGrade 10 ELA and Mathematics results exclude students repeating grade 10 who previously participated in the same subject test. High school Science participation reflects testing in grades 9 or 10 and varies by year: since 2024, it includes Biology and Introductory Physics; prior to 2024, it includes Biology, Chemistry, Introductory Physics, and Technology/Engineering.\n\nParticipation rates are not reported for groups with fewer than 10 enrolled students. English learners are counted as participants only if they meet both MCAS ELA testing requirements and complete the ACCESS for ELLs assessment.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site:\n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/participation.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MCAS Participation</a>",
